[I] A implementation of a Fortran front end written in modern C++

[T] Flang is a ground-up implementation of a Fortran front end written in
[T] modern C++. It started off as the f18 project and replacethe previous
[T] flang project.

[U] https://llvm.org/

[A] University of Illinois/NCSA
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/development
[F] OBJDIR CROSS F77
[R] + arm64 loongarch64 powerpc powerpc64 riscv64 sparc sparc64 x86 x86-64

[L] BSD
[V] 23.1.4

[CV-GROUP] llvm-project
[D] 6c929d73fedd5035751b0365f5740abd57ff803d4abe67690f90726d llvm-project-23.1.4.src.tar.xz https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/releases/download/llvmorg-23.1.4/

srcdir=*/flang

var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DFLANG_INCLUDE_TESTS=OFF

cmake_mod() {
        tar $taropt `match_source_file -p cmake` -C ..
        mv -vf ../cmake-*src ../../cmake
}
hook_add preconf 5 cmake_mod
